wifi: 11: at the end of the watch the DSP's item says: SMP2P version 1, features 0x1, from processor 13 to 0, flags 0, 3 of 16 entries: smp2p = 0; slave-kernel = 0x6; wlan = 0;
wifi: 11: and ours: SMP2P version 1, features 0x1, from processor 0 to 13, flags 0, 2 of 16 entries: master-kernel = 0; wlan = 0;
wifi: 11: the watch is over after 261 ms; doorbells heard: GLINK 1, SMP2P 1, the mailbox 1, others 0
wifi: 11: the DSP said it was up, and that it has asked for its own power
wifi: step 12: find GLINK's descriptor and the two queues in the shared memory, and read what the DSP has put into its own (nothing is taken out)
wifi: 12: our queue: 16384 bytes at 0x809c5060, written to 0, read by the DSP to 0; the DSP's: 16384 bytes at 0x809c9208, written to 0x8, read by us to 0
wifi: 12:   in the DSP's queue at 0: version 1 0x7 
wifi: step 13: take up GLINK with the DSP: our version into our queue and its doorbell, then whatever its messages call for (writes: our queue, our two marks in the descriptor, the doorbell); a thread of ours listens from here on, every millisecond
